#### 7. Assertion Roulette

**File:** `OrderProcessorTests.cs` · **Method:** `CalculateTotal_ReturnsCorrectAmount` (lines 84–86)

```csharp
Assert.AreEqual(247.50m, order.TotalAmount);
Assert.AreEqual(22.28m, order.TaxAmount);
Assert.AreEqual(269.78m, order.GrandTotal);
```

**Problem:** 3 assertions with no message parameters. When one fails, the MSTest output shows expected vs. actual but gives no indication of *which business value* was wrong — "TotalAmount", "TaxAmount", or "GrandTotal"?

**Fix — add descriptive messages:**

```csharp
Assert.AreEqual(expectedSubtotal, order.TotalAmount, "Subtotal mismatch");
Assert.AreEqual(expectedTax, order.TaxAmount, "Tax amount mismatch");
Assert.AreEqual(expectedSubtotal + expectedTax, order.GrandTotal, "Grand total mismatch");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Time wasted reading source to identify which assertion failed.

